UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The King of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Mastery"—the apex of the fire element where the sovereign consciousness has fully matured into a visionary, long-term architect of its own manifest reality. Moving beyond the radiant presence of the Queen, the King signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Visionary," where your creative power is no longer merely a field you inhabit, but a structured, legacy-building instrument you actively command. Visually depicted as a king seated on a throne decorated with salamanders and lions, holding a blossoming staff, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Stewardship"—the realization that true power is the ability to leverage your creative fire to build, sustain, and defend a reality that serves not just your own ego, but the long-term thriving of your entire, chosen ecosystem. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Strategic Synthesis," where your impulses, your magnetism, and your actions have harmonized into a coherent, enduring, and authoritative blueprint for existence. When the King of Wands appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Sovereign" status; you are the undisputed author of your domain, and you are being invited to take full responsibility for the structure of your life. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your legacy. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Authorship": moving past the need for external validation or temporary excitement, and dedicating your energy to the construction of a foundation that will stand the test of time. To inhabit the King of Wands is to master the art of "Sovereign Stewardship," recognizing that by directing your creative fire with the cold, clear eye of a master, you are effectively transforming your life from a series of accidental events into a deliberate, intentional, and sovereign work of art.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the King of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Tyranny," "Visionary-Collapse," or the catastrophic—yet curative—failure to manage the power you have claimed, leading to a state of aggressive, controlling, and fundamentally unstable volatility. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "dominance" with "leadership," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a critical, ego-driven fracture of its original mission. You are essentially "burning down your own kingdom," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s need for total control and external submission over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually serve the vision you once claimed to protect. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "absolute ruler," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of isolation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "ruling over a ruin," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your "authority" is built upon the fear and compliance of those around you, rather than their genuine respect. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of ego-inflation"; you are obsessively trying to force your will upon the environment, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final dismantling of your tyranny is your own, deep-seated fear that without the power to command, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, hollow state. The reversed King of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of loss of control, and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "mighty leader" and return to the silence of your own, unvalidated work, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these authoritarian, control-seeking scripts, perform a brutal audit of your leadership style, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your vision over the comfort of your command. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical decentralization—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "ruling" over the vulnerability of "serving," and realizing that until you are willing to let the throne crumble and stand in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, honest truth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom authority you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 28;
